    "task_design_summary": {
      "detailed_description": "Read the JSON inventory on the first Linux device. The JSON contains a list of product records (product_id, name, version, status). Select only records where status == \"approved\". On the second Linux device there is an ODP template deck containing a template slide titled \"Template Slide: Product Summary\" with text anchors for PRODUCT_ID, PRODUCT_NAME, VERSION, STATUS. For each approved product, create a new slide based on that template slide and populate the anchors with the product's product_id, name, version, and status. Save the resulting ODP deck as /home/user/presentations/product_updates.odp. The required output semantics: the saved deck must contain one Product Summary slide per approved product from the JSON and each such slide must include deterministic text anchors with the Product ID, Name, Version and Status values taken from the JSON. In addition, the saved presentation's document title must include the phrase \"Product Updates\" so that the presentation title is clearly identifiable as the product updates deck. The expected_data values (product IDs, names, versions, statuses) are directly taken from the JSON source; the mapping to slides is determined by the presence of the template slide anchors in the template ODP on the second device.",
